{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520153-v5-homebrew-ventrue-antitribu-loresheet-redux","id":1520153,"title":"(V5 homebrew) Ventrue antitribu loresheet, redux","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-08T15:03:43-07:00","id":1520153,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon8.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> (V5 homebrew) Ventrue antitribu loresheet, redux","content":"<i>Good lord</i>, what is up with this auto-flagging stuff since I came back to the forums? Anyhow, here's a repost, <i>I guess</i>.<br /> <br /> I love Ventrue <i>antitribu</i>, and thought I'd start working up a homebrew loresheet for them. I'd be interested in hearing thoughts, suggestions, balancing concerns, and vibe checks about the whole thing. What I'm presenting at first will be a brainstorm WIP, so bear in mind. My own commentary is in italics.<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of the Blood (Ventrue only)</b><br /> <br /> Rawr we still think it's the 1200's! We don't bring knives to gunfights, we bring swords! Really, really big swords! The two most important words in the English language to us are DEUS, and VULT. In that order. The other Ventrue may think we're atavistic throwbacks and Renaissance Faire LARP'ers, but to that we say LARP DEEZ NUTS.<br /> <br /> <i>(Yeah, I'm shitposting fluff at this point. I need to suss out mechanics first.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Squire of the Knights:</b> You have been initiated into the Knights of the Blood, and are learning to discern the machinations of the Ephorate. If this merit is bought at character creation, you may reallocate a single discipline dot from Dominate or Presence to Auspex; otherwise, you may purchase your first dot of Auspex without having tasted the blood of a vampire with it (you must still feed from mortals of Phlegmatic resonance).<br /> <br /> <i>(Yay, &quot;free&quot; Auspex without having to give up Presence or Dominate, since v5 is -- probably rightly -- anti-&quot;extra clan discipline&quot; shenanigans. But still out-of-clan at this point, if the player wants to hold on to both Dominate and Presence without giving up bloodline flavor. I'm entirely aware this would allow the character to start with Auspex 2 with the right predator type, and that's on purpose.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Schemes of the Masters:</b> Your experience acting as an inquisitor towards your own clan has granted you insight into their methods and goals, and how they relate to the Ephorate and the clan at large. Once per story, you may ask your Storyteller for a single piece of information about the Ventrue in your own city or those nearby, and be given an accurate answer. As a consequence of your actions against your own clan, you gain the Status flaw <b>(</b>\u2022<b>) Suspect</b> with Ventrue loyal to the Camarilla, regardless of your Status with other groups.<br /> <br /> <i>(&quot;Ask Storyteller for X information&quot; seems to be a running theme with two-dot loresheet merits, and I'm not breaking the mold here. If you're taking this loresheet to begin with, you're probably interested in fucking the Ventrue in particular, and free information about local Ventrue and their weaknesses is just the thing for it.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Crusader's Armory: </b>Experience has taught you the surest way to fail in your duties is to be unprepared, and you are rarely without the tools you need to see your duties done. Havens which you inhabit, including temporary and shared havens, gain two dots to split between Hidden Armory, Library, and Security System at your choice. Your hidden armories may also include melee weapons, bows, crossbows, and stakes instead of pistols or long firearms, at your discretion. Additionally, add two dice to Preparedness checks you make.<br /> <br /> <i>(Archaic weapons are just plain better against vampires than firearms, and these vamps know that as well as anyone else -- if not better. Even if their possession risks the Masquerade. Having weapons and texts squirreled away everywhere, and being a vampiric MacGuyver with always having the right tool for the job, fits the &quot;rough and always ready&quot; archetype so well.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Blessed by St. Gustav: </b>You have either participated in the Prayer to St. Gustav rite, or your sire did prior to your Embrace. Select either Dominate or Presence to replace with Auspex as an in-clan discipline. You retain whatever dots you had in the replaced discipline, but you buy additional dots at out-of-clan cost. If you retain Presence, you may not possess the Awe, Entrancement, or Star Magnetism powers; if you already had those powers, you must replace them with Daunt, Dread Gaze, or Majesty respectively. Your associations come at cost, however: you gain the Status flaw <b>(</b>\u2022\u2022<b>) Shunned</b> with Ventrue loyal to the Camarilla, regardless of your Status with other groups.<br /> <br /> <i>(And here we have it, that which defines the Knights of Blood and/or Ventrue antitribu: in-clan Auspex. Except here, because VtR's Nightmare discipline was folded into VtM Presence, I'm letting them keep it at the cost of giving up Dominate. Loading up with the &quot;Nightmare&quot; powers better fits the whole &quot;scary monstrous vampire warlord&quot; archetype the Ventrue antitribu embody better than Dominate, in my opinion. But, they can still keep Dominate if they want.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Duty Before Dishonor: </b>Your dedication to the order, and resolve to see the Ephorate undone once and for all, is unwavering. You grieve the sacrifices you make to achieve that greater good, and move on stronger for the experience. Once per story, you may choose to automatically succeed a Remorse check if any of your Stains were acquired in service to one of your Convictions, or to further your Ambition.<br /> <br /> <i>(The Ventrue antitribu are/were a Sabbat bloodline, and that means doing some heinous shit in contradiction with &quot;knightly&quot; values. Modern nights existence means doing shit in contradiction with &quot;knightly&quot; values. Even &quot;knightly&quot; values as twisted through the hypocritical lens of the Sabbat. You gotta learn to reconcile that, get over your shit, and move on -- and this merit reflects the learned capacity to do so.)</i>\u200b<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> One thing I'm considering after giving it a sleep, is getting rid of the current two-dot merit, slightly nerfing and shifting the three-dot merit down to two, and replacing it with another. So, it would look like this:<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Crusader's Armory:</b> Experience taught you unpreparedness is the surest way to fail in your duties, and you are never far from the tools you need to see them done. Havens which you inhabit, including temporary and shared havens, gain a free dot in either Hidden Armory or Security System at your choice. Your hidden armories may include melee weapons, bows, crossbows, and stakes instead of pistols and long firearms. Additionally, add two dice to your dice pool when making Preparedness checks.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Victori Spolia</b><b>:</b> Contests and victory are part of a crusader's (un)lifeblood, and you have adapted to claim your due from those you have bested. If you defeat a mortal in physical or social combat and they are not your preferred victim, you may feed from them without spending Willpower. If mortals you defeat in combat are your preferred victim, slake an additional Hunger when feeding from them (you must still kill your victim to reduce Hunger to zero).<br /> <br /> <i>(This really puts Ventrue antitribu in their rightful place as the &quot;evil twin&quot; of warrior-caste Salubri. It could also have cool synergy, role-playing, and story hook possibilities for Ventrue antitribu whose predator types are alleycat, montero, pursuer, roadside killer, or trapdoor -- emphasizing and incentivizing a more violent and martial feeding style than that associated with the Blue Bloods.)</i><br /> <br /> Also, instead of the five-dot merit being a once-per-story &quot;get out of degeneration free&quot; card, I'm thinking this:<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Duty Before Dishonor: </b>Your dedication to the order, and resolve to see the Ephorate undone once and for all, is unwavering. Sacrifices have to be made in the name of the greater good. If you acquire Stains as the result of a bestial failure or messy critical, and your Convictions would mitigate a single Stain, you instead mitigate them all.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T09:22:42-07:00","id":1520212,"title":"","content":"I certainly like the care you put into your loresheet and this is someone who doesn't play Ventrue characters at all and I can't think of any real suggestions on how you can improve it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T17:37:56-08:00","id":1527613,"title":"","content":"Bit of a necro, but having played around a little more with what else is on tap with v5, I thought I'd revisit and see if I could make it a little bit more apropos and thematic.<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of the Blood (Ventrue only)</b><br /> <br /> Still fluff shitpost, but a second thought on it. When the Sabbat launched the Gehenna crusade, the handful of Ventrue <i>antitribu</i> with their wits about them defected to the Anarchs, making up a bunch of BS about how the Gehenna crusade is actually what the Secret Masters want. They worked with the few number of Anarch Ventrue out and about, to revitalize and rebirth the actual Knights of the Blood as an internal organization dedicated to warring against the Camarilla, Inner Council, and Ephorate.<br /> <br /> I also thought it would be fun and appropriate, if this is an Anarch Ventrue faction, for them to venerate Jurgen von Verden opposed to Gustav Mallenhous. At least, openly -- I figure the ones &quot;in the know&quot; would still venerate Gustav, and pass the Prayer to St. Gustav rite around.<br /> <br /> Jurgen was, after all, the Ventrue warlord who bested many of the mightiest Cainites of the Dark Ages, who stayed true to the Ventrue's &quot;true&quot; mission, and for his efforts was cruelly martyred by Hardestadt in order to pave way for &quot;kinder and softer&quot; generations of Ventrue. After all, that's the way it looks if you squint hard enough and have Dominate, Presence, and the blood bond to &quot;convince&quot; others he was the true hero, all along.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Oaths of the Black Cross:</b> As an initiate to the Knights, you have taken oaths sanctified by blood and rite to uphold virtues held sacred by your forebears. You adopt a new Conviction directly related to knightly virtues, such as &quot;never break a sworn oath&quot;, &quot;never show cowardice&quot;, or &quot;always answer challenges to your honor&quot;. This Conviction does not apply towards your maximum of three Convictions, and you do not have to discard any other Conviction to adopt it. You do not have to have a Touchstone connected to this Conviction, and you cannot lose this Conviction as the result of losing an associated Touchstone. However, if you violate this Conviction, you gain one or more Stains as if you had violated a Chronicle Tenet; these Stains cannot be mitigated by other Convictions.<br /> <br /> <i>(Honestly, this is just a little more unique and thematically appropriate, than &quot;you can fuck around with Auspex&quot;. Fucking around with Auspex comes later. An extra Conviction with different strings attached -- it functions for the character as an additional Chronicle Tenet, but without the baggage of a Touchstone -- adds a lot more dynamism and potential roleplay benefits/challenges/risks to a character whose player would take this.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Crusader's Armory:</b> Experience taught you unpreparedness is the surest way to fail in your duties, and you are never far from the tools you need to see them done. Havens which you inhabit, including temporary and shared havens, gain a free dot in either Hidden Armory or Security System at your choice. Your hidden armories may include melee weapons, bows, crossbows, and stakes instead of pistols and long firearms. Additionally, add two dice to your dice pool when making Preparedness checks.<br /> <br /> <i>(I still like this, and think it fits the bill.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Victori Spolia</b><b>:</b> Contests and victory are part of a crusader's (un)lifeblood, and you have adapted to claim your due from those you have bested. If you defeat a mortal in fair physical or social combat and they are not your preferred victim, you may feed from them without spending Willpower. If mortals you defeat in combat are your preferred victim, slake an additional Hunger when feeding (you must still kill your victim to reduce Hunger to zero).<br /> <br /> <i>(I still like this, too. But, I added the &quot;fair&quot; disclaimer to ensure players wouldn't just go around ganking victims Alleycat-style, and thereby bypass the Ventrue feeding restriction entirely. Plus, this reinforces the whole &quot;pseudo-Road of Kings&quot; flair the one-dot merit brings.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Blessed by St. Gustav: </b>You have either participated in the Prayer to St. Gustav rite, or your sire did prior to your Embrace. Add Auspex to your list of innate disciplines, but you do not have experience points already spent for Auspex powers refunded. However, you may not possess the Presence powers of Awe, Entrancement, or Star Magnetism; if you already possessed them at the time of taking this merit, replace them with other Presence powers of equivalent or lower level.\u200b<br /> <br /> <i>(I just bought the bullet and did the whole &quot;extra clan discipline&quot; thing. After the whole bloodline-specific Hecata discipline thing...you know what, fuck it. I'm still not letting them &quot;play nice&quot; with Presence, though.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Vox Imperatoris:</b> Your identity as a crusader and your presence at the forefront of any battle has the capability to inspire those who follow you to incredible acts of courage and valor. When you use a Potence or Fortitude power in combat, or a Potence or Fortitude power affects an action you take, you may make an additional Rouse Check for a single ally to gain two bonus dice on their next action or roll to resist Frenzy. Alternatively, when using an action to command another or use teamwork in combat, you may make a Rouse Check to give a single ally bonus dice equal to your Presence rating in lieu of the normal teamwork bonus.<br /> <br /> <i>(Since in this rework I already had one merit dedicated to Convictions, Stains, and Humanity, I'm trying another tact for a five-dot merit. Being I love Give 'em Hell/Inspire Greatness, I thought I'd try my hand at reworking it for v5 mechanics. This is pretty much my attempt at it, which I figure is thematically appropriate and in line with other five-dot loresheet merits.)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T14:52:11-08:00","id":1527640,"title":"","content":"I actually quit being a mod because I couldn't deal with the deluge of autoflagged posts.<br /> <br /> Fantastic Loresheets!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}